-- title:
--   Level preservation cut out by a finitely generated ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$, a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, a natural number $N$, a commutative ring $S$, and two fake elliptic curves $E,A$ over $S$ of type `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S` (each consisting of a scheme with a structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} S$, a commutative relative group law, an abelian-scheme property bundle, fibres of topological Krull dimension $2$, an action of $\Lambda$ by endomorphisms over the base compatible with the group law and with the prescribed trace condition, together with a level scheme and its morphism `lev` into the total space and the finiteness, flatness, finite-presentation and closed-immersion properties recorded in the structure). Let $\varphi : E.A \to A.A$ be a scheme morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} S$, i.e. $\varphi$ followed by $A.f$ equals $E.f$. The assertion is that there exists a finitely generated ideal $J \subseteq S$ with the following property: for every commutative ring $T$, every ring homomorphism $\psi : S \to T$, every pair of fake elliptic curves $E',A'$ over $T$, and every pair of morphisms $g_E : E'.A \to E.A$, $g_A : A'.A \to A.A$ exhibiting $E'$ and $A'$ as base changes of $E$ and $A$ along $\psi$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsPullbackVia` (the square formed by $g_E$, $E'.f$, $E.f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}\psi$ is a pullback, $g_E$ carries the relative group law of $E'$ to that of $E$ on points over any base, $E'.act\,x$ followed by $g_E$ equals $g_E$ followed by $E.act\,x$ for all $x \in \Lambda$, and every point of $E'$ factoring through $E'.lev$ has its image under $g_E$ factoring through $E.lev$; similarly for $g_A$), and every $\varphi' : E'.A \to A'.A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} T$ with $\varphi'$ followed by $g_A$ equal to $g_E \circ \varphi$, one has: $\varphi'$ preserves level, meaning that for every scheme $T_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec} T$ and every point $P$ of $E'$ over it which factors through $E'.lev$, the point $P$ followed by $\varphi'$ factors through $A'.lev$, if and only if the ideal generated by $\psi(J)$ in $T$ is zero.
--
--   This is the representability of the level-preservation condition for a morphism of fake elliptic curves by a closed subscheme of the base which is cut out by a finitely generated ideal: a single ideal $J$ of $S$ governs, simultaneously and independently of the chosen base changes, whether the base-changed morphism carries the level structure of $E$ into that of $A$ over every $S$-algebra. It is used in the construction of the scheme of isogeny pairs for the Čerednik–Drinfel'd moduli problem, where it feeds into the statement that the level-preservation locus is a closed immersion locally of finite presentation.
